WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:11.059
It was the only thing on the page we did not paint.

2
00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:22.234
Someone folded it from a page of homework, and set it down where the rain was going.

3
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:34.056
A boat made of paper, in a street made of rain.

4
00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:54.283
We painted the street ahead of it. The kerb, the lamp, the shop that sells everything.

5
00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:10.829
We gave it a number: day 1, 0 kilometres. It gave us nothing back.

6
00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:32.052
Where the street ended, the water went under the road, and we could not follow with a brush.

7
00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:50.671
You cannot paint what you cannot see. So for a while, the page was the sound of water.

8
00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:14.524
It came out the other side a little greyer, and still a boat.

9
00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:41.134
Day 1 ended at a canal, which is a river that someone has argued with.

10
00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:11.421
In the morning there were reeds, and a bridge, and a crow on the bridge who had opinions.

11
00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:34.749
We painted the world one bend at a time, and it kept going.

12
00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:55.577
The crow followed. Crows follow anything that might turn out to be food.

13
00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:12.896
We measured. It did not care.

14
00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:26.138
Then it stopped.

15
00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:45.416
A dam of leaves, the size of a hand, and a whole voyage behind it.

16
00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:03.840
We waited. The paint dried. The crow left.

17
00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:32.281
And the sky, which had started this, started it again.

18
00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:23.199
We had never painted the dark. The dark is mostly what you leave out.

19
00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:48.213
That night the canal ran past a town, and the town was putting lights on the water.

20
00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:18.630
Hundreds of them. Small flames on leaf cups, set down by people we could not see.

21
00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:43.442
For an hour the boat had company. It did not seem to notice that either.

22
00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:17.296
One by one the lamps went out, the way lamps do, from the oldest.

23
00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:44.963
By morning it was alone again, which is to say, it was itself.

24
00:08:55.850 --> 00:09:00.475
Day 3. 5 kilometres. We drew the number small.

25
00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:20.941
The crow came back at breakfast.

26
00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:35.830
It had decided that the boat was a kind of bread.

27
00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:52.655
It lifted it, and for the first time the boat left the water.

28
00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:19.825
From up there the canal was a line, and the town was a smudge, and the river ahead was a wide blue promise.

29
00:10:35.850 --> 00:10:39.928
We painted it all. We had been waiting for a reason.

30
00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:57.874
Then the crow worked out what paper tastes like.

31
00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:20.353
It dropped the boat into a flooded field, where the sky lay on the ground in squares.

32
00:11:39.850 --> 00:11:46.742
It had travelled 4 kilometres in a minute, and learned nothing. That is the right way to travel.

33
00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:19.956
On the fourth day the monsoon stopped pretending.

34
00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:37.057
The field drained into the river, and the river had somewhere to be.

35
00:12:53.850 --> 00:13:00.828
Things went past. A slipper. A cricket ball. A tree that had been standing an hour ago.

36
00:13:25.850 --> 00:13:30.230
We painted a rock, to steer it. It went over the rock.

37
00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:53.800
The weir.

38
00:14:07.850 --> 00:14:13.933
It came down sideways, and lost the tip of its sail, and kept going with less.

39
00:14:29.850 --> 00:14:34.253
We had thought it was whole before. It was only complete.

40
00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:54.637
20 kilometres by dark. We stopped noting the time.

41
00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:23.205
Day 5 was a lake, and a lake is a river with nothing to say.

42
00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:44.805
Nothing moved. The boat sat on its own reflection all morning.

43
00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:16.526
We painted everything around it. A heron. Dragonflies. The far shore, twice.

44
00:16:51.850 --> 00:16:55.830
We painted wind. That is not how wind works.

45
00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:16.427
So we put the brush down.

46
00:17:31.850 --> 00:17:34.659
It was the first time we had.

47
00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:49.983
And something that was not us moved the water.

48
00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:31.558
The river entered a city at dusk, and the city was already full of boats.

49
00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:50.666
Painted ones. Wooden, iron, with names and lamps and men who shouted across the water.

50
00:18:59.850 --> 00:19:05.541
Among a thousand painted things, one unpainted thing is hard to see.

51
00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:34.206
A ship went past that took a whole minute to go past.

52
00:20:15.850 --> 00:20:24.440
The crow was there, on a rail, older. It looked at the boat and did nothing. That is what friendship is, in crows.

53
00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:55.541
The city put its lights on the water too, but these ones did not go out.

54
00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:17.531
110 kilometres. The ink was running low. So were we.

55
00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:43.720
At dawn the river stopped being a river, the way a sentence stops at the end.

56
00:21:59.850 --> 00:22:07.073
We had painted ahead of it for seven days. The kerb, the dark, the lamps, the flood, the city.

57
00:22:19.850 --> 00:22:22.136
Here, we did not.

58
00:22:41.850 --> 00:22:49.163
We left the page blank, and the boat went into the blank, because that is what it had been doing all along.

59
00:23:15.850 --> 00:23:19.908
When the paint dried, the world we made was gone.

60
00:23:37.850 --> 00:23:41.528
Only the part we left alone arrived.
